# ☁️ Cloud & SaaS Subscription Sprawl — AI-Powered BI Platform

**AICTE | IBM SkillsBuild Data Analytics with AI Internship 2026 (BharatCares)**
**Author:** Mohammad Ayan Ansari — Indian Institute of Technology, Madras
**Trainer:** Mr. Kartik Hooda | **Mode:** Online | **Date:** September 2026

## 📌 Overview
Enterprises lose 30–40% of SaaS spend to unused licenses, duplicate tools (Slack + Teams + Zoom), and risky auto-renewals.
This project converts **600 raw SaaS subscriptions into a decision platform** that answers:

> What are we spending? Where is it wasted? Why? What is the risk? What should we DO?

**Business Intelligence flow:** Data → KPIs → Trends → Drivers → Risks & Opportunities → Recommended Actions.

## 🎯 Key Results (on included dataset)
- **Monthly Spend:** $1,126,679 | **Annual Contract:** $12,717,123
- **Monthly Waste:** $447,613 (**39.7%** of spend) — 168/600 subs <40% utilized
- **Avg Utilization:** 59.8% | **High-risk renewals:** 64
- **AI Model (Random Forest, waste prediction):** Accuracy **97.5%**, Precision 94.3%, Recall 97.1%, F1 95.7%

## 🗂️ Dataset
- **File:** `dataset_saas_sprawl.csv` (600 rows × 22 columns)
- **Source:** Synthetic dataset generated for this project, modelled on real-world SaaS patterns
  (patterns inspired by public Kaggle SaaS / subscription datasets). No masterclass learning dataset used.
- **Dataset link (this repo):** _paste your GitHub repo link here after upload, e.g._
  `https://github.com/<your-username>/saas-sprawl-bi/blob/main/dataset_saas_sprawl.csv`
- **Columns:** Subscription_ID, Owner_ID, Department, SaaS_Tool, Category, Plan_Type,
  Cost_Per_License_Month, Licenses_Purchased, Licenses_Used, Utilization_Pct,
  Last_Login_Days_Ago, Renewal_Date, Annual_Contract_Value, Monthly_Spend,
  Auto_Renew, Status, Region, Unused_Licenses, Waste_Monthly, Waste_Flag,
  Days_to_Renewal, Renewal_Risk

## 🏗️ Architecture
- **Backend:** Python + Pandas (cleaning/EDA) + Scikit-learn RandomForest (waste prediction)
- **Frontend:** Streamlit (5 pages) + Plotly (interactive charts) — **single file `app.py`**
- **Pages:**
  1. Executive Overview (Top KPIs)
  2. Cost & Product Analysis (waste by tool, duplicates)
  3. Risk & Renewal Analysis (≤90-day renewals, high-risk table + CSV export)
  4. AI Waste Predictor (live prediction + feature importance)
  5. Fact → Action Board (30-60-90 day playbook)

## ⚙️ Tech Stack
Python, Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-learn, Streamlit, Plotly, Matplotlib, Seaborn

## 🚀 Quick Start (localhost)
```bash
# 1. Clone / download this repo, keep app.py + dataset_saas_sprawl.csv together
# 2. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 3. Run the app
streamlit run app.py
# Open http://localhost:8501 in your browser
```

## 📊 How to Use
1. Use sidebar filters (Department / Category / Risk) — all KPIs & charts update.
2. Page 1: read headline KPIs + spend trend.
3. Page 2: find top waste tools & duplicate stacks to consolidate.
4. Page 3: download high-risk renewals CSV before auto-renew dates.
5. Page 4: enter any new subscription → AI predicts Wasteful / Efficient.
6. Page 5: copy the 30-60-90 day action playbook for management.

## 🧠 Model Details
- **Target:** `Waste_Flag` = 1 if Utilization < 40% & Active
- **Features:** cost, licenses, utilization, dormancy, contract value, days-to-renewal, unused seats + one-hot(Category, Plan_Type, Auto_Renew, Department)
- **Split:** 80/20 stratified, seed 42 | **Model:** RandomForest (200 trees, depth 12, balanced)
- **Top drivers:** Utilization_Pct, Unused_Licenses, Licenses_Used, Last_Login_Days_Ago, Monthly_Spend

